      "edition": "Sunday 27 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Domestic URC",
          "heading": "Zebre Parma Falls To Seven-Try Bulls In Opening URC Defeat",
          "body": "Zebre suffered a heavy 47-13 defeat against the Bulls in their United Rugby Championship opener in Parma on Saturday. Despite an early penalty goal from Tommaso Allan, the hosts struggled to maintain momentum after Matteo Canali was sent to the sin-bin. Captain Alessandro Fusco provided a moment of individual brilliance in the final quarter, stepping through the defence to score, but the visitors proved too clinical, crossing for seven tries to secure a dominant victory on the road."
        },
