    "390": {
      "date": "2026-09-27",
      "edition": "Sunday 27 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "URC triumph",
          "heading": "Glasgow bench inspires dramatic second-half comeback victory against Munster",
          "body": "Glasgow Warriors secured a 26-20 victory over Munster at Thomond Park in Saturday's opening round of the United Rugby Championship. Despite trailing by 10 points at the interval, the visitors clawed their way back through a second-half resurgence. The introduction of the Scottish bench proved decisive, providing the necessary impact to dismantle the Munster defence. Tries from Nathan McBeth, George Horne, and a late score from Horne himself ensured the Warriors departed Limerick with a hard-fought bonus-point win."
        },
