      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "WXV result",
          "heading": "Wales women suffer narrow defeat against USA in Cardiff contest",
          "body": "Wales women fell to a 26-24 defeat against a clinical USA side at Cardiff Arms Park on Saturday. Despite scoring tries through Keira Bevan, Kelsey Jones, Sisilia Tuipulotu and Alex Callender, the hosts were undone by an error-strewn performance and a hat-trick from Eagles number eight Freda Tafuna. Head coach Sean Lynn remained positive regarding his side's resilience, noting: \"I saw some grit, I saw some effort there,\" as the team now turns its attention to next month’s fixtures against Japan."
        },
